import Sheaf.RingTheory.CohenRing

/-!
# Existence of Cohen rings

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 0328
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-cohen-rings-exist).
-/

universe u

/-- Every field of prime characteristic is the residue field of a Cohen ring.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 0328.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-cohen-rings-exist)

Proof plan (the ten steps of the DAG node):
1. The p-adic integers form a Cohen ring with residue field F_p
   [def-weil-l-adic-numbers].
2. Choose a flat local Z_p-algebra R with maximal ideal pR and residue field k
   [lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-extension-given-residue-field, Stacks 03C3].
3. Complete R at pR. The completion Λ is Noetherian, complete, nonzero, and Λ/pΛ ≃ k
   [def-weil-pbc-adic-completion, def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring,
   lem-weil-pbc-completion-noetherian-quotient-noetherian,
   lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-mod-ideal, def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring].
4. Completeness puts pΛ in the Jacobson radical; the field quotient makes Λ local with
   maximal ideal pΛ [lem-weil-pbc-adic-complete-jacobson-radical].
5. The pR-adic and p^nR-adic filtrations are cofinal, so Λ/p^nΛ ≃ R/p^nR
   [lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-mod-ideal].
6. Flatness of Z_p → R gives flatness of Z/p^n → R/p^nR, hence of Z/p^n → Λ/p^nΛ
   [lem-weil-pbc-flat-module-base-change, def-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map].
7. The complete flatness criterion gives flatness of Z_p → Λ
   [lem-weil-pbc-flat-module-powers].
8. Flatness preserves injectivity of multiplication by p; p and its powers are nonzero
   nonzerodivisors [def-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map].
9. Separatedness gives intersection of p^nΛ equal to zero. For nonzero x, choose the largest
   n with x in p^nΛ; write x = p^n u. Maximality makes u a unit
   [def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring].
10. Such factorizations show Λ is a domain and every nonzero ideal is generated by the least
    occurring power of p. Thus Λ is a local PID, not a field, complete with uniformizer p,
    and its quotient is k [def-weil-pbc-cohen-ring, def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring]. -/
theorem exists_cohenRing (p : ℕ) (hp : Nat.Prime p) (k : Type u) [Field k] [CharP k p] :
    ∃ (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ),
      IsCohenRing p Λ ∧ Nonempty ((Λ ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : Λ)}) ≃+* k) := by
  sorry
